# Upstream: github.com/<your-github-username>/claudes-markdown-12-rules/.gitignore
# Everything above the scaffold block below is that file, verbatim. Re-pull it
# rather than hand-editing here, so one project's fix reaches every project.

# Dependencies
**/node_modules/

# Lock files (never change, never need context)
**/package-lock.json
**/go.sum
**/poetry.lock
**/Cargo.lock

# Build output
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/build/
**/target/

# Binary / compiled
# **/bin/ was here from the shared ignore set (compiled output). In this repo every
# tree keeps its scripts in bin/ (graph/bin/graph.sh, events/bin/event.sh,
# queue/bin/queue.sh, roles/bin/render-playbook.sh, bin/). The line silently kept
# all of them out of PR #1: main had no scripts and `make lint` could not run.
# Removed 2026-10-10 UTC. Compiled output goes under dist/ or target/, never bin/.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Stale branches
**/.worktrees/

# IDE / cache
**/.superpowers/
**/.claude/agents/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/node_modules/.cache

# Test coverage / reports
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
**/htmlcov/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Env files (security + noise)
**/.env*
!**/.env.example

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs/

# Terraform state / cache / secrets
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# Docker layer cache
**/.dockercache/

# Python venvs
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Temp / scratch
**/tmp/
**/temp/

# Vim swap files
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*.un~

# OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- project-scaffold ------------------------------------------------------
# Not upstream's concern: the files this skill's tools create.

# installed skills - copies, owned by skill-sync, replaced on every session start
#
# The blanket mirrors `**/.claude/agents/` in the upstream block above, and lives
# down here rather than beside it on purpose: everything above this line is
# re-pulled verbatim, so a line added there is dropped by the next re-pull with
# no conflict and no warning. This is the only thing stopping a skill copy from
# being committed, and a project that commits one gets a copy that never updates
# again while `registry.json` moves on without it.
**/.claude/skills/

# agent cache - derived, rebuildable, never authoritative
.claude/cache/

# local settings - machine-specific paths, recreated by scaffold.sh
.claude/settings.local.json

# lock files used by the scaffold tools
.issues.lock

# generated aggregates and per-seat state: never tracked, so no pull request can carry them. WO-20261012-0677.
# What broke: CHANGELOG.md, work-orders/INDEX.md, the epic and archive READMEs and CONTEXT_STATE.md were tracked, and every PR
# rewrote them (work-order start, submit and done reindex; make step renders the changelog and appends a checkpoint), so
# each merge forced the next PR into a conflict, a main merge and a full re-test (PRs 25, 28, 29, 30, 31 on 2026-10-12).
# Why this fix: ignored files cannot ride a diff, and each is rebuilt from tracked sources by `make aggregates` (the
# changelog from changelog/, the index and READMEs from the tickets). CONTEXT_STATE.md is the seat's own sliding window,
# read in place by resume-checkpoint.sh. Rejected: rendering after merge from the merger seat (its role file is off limits
# to a worker and a skipped render leaves main wrong). Cost: github.com no longer shows CHANGELOG.md or INDEX.md, and a
# fresh slot starts with no checkpoint file. factory/bin/claims.sh diff still refuses them if one is force-added.
# Placed here, not at the end of the file, so it does not sit next to the lines other PRs append there.
/CHANGELOG.md
/CONTEXT_STATE.md
/work-orders/INDEX.md
/work-orders/**/README.md
.backlog.lock

# runtime work queue state (queue/bin/queue.sh), never committed
queue/items/

# the factory board's drawn page and data (report/loop/loop.sh watch): derived from the records, rebuilt on every change
report/loop/out/
# route runner state (factory/bin/route.sh): the routed ledger, the first-start boundary and the belt file. WO-20261011-38c7.
# What it would break if committed: every runner start in another checkout would read this checkout's ledger and either
# skip records it never saw or route ones already routed. Runtime state, never committed, same as queue/items/ above.
factory/state/
report/blueprint/out/
